### 5.3 Quick command and payload safety notes

- Do not run arbitrary operating-system commands on a live target to test SSTI.
- Do not read application secrets or unrelated users' information.
- Do not use high-volume fuzzing where it may disrupt a service.
- Keep intrusive engine-capability testing inside a local or intentionally vulnerable lab.
- Never store unredacted session tokens in notes or public reports.

