## 11. 🧠 Must-Remember Cheat Sheet

| Concept | Remember |
|---|---|
| SSTI | Untrusted input is evaluated as template code |
| Primary CWE | CWE-1336 |
| Detection | Baseline + harmless expression + server-side confirmation |
| Reflection | Not sufficient evidence |
| Engine identification | Use multiple indicators |
| RCE | Possible, not guaranteed |
| Root cause | Unsafe template construction or evaluation |
| Primary fix | Fixed template + user input as data |
| Defense in depth | Least privilege, sandboxing, isolation, updates |
| Reporting | Reproducible proof and impact supported by evidence |

### Final mental model

**SSTI is fundamentally a code-versus-data separation failure in server-side template rendering.**

A strong researcher does not just find an expression that evaluates. They establish where the evaluation happens, understand the application's security boundary, validate impact responsibly, eliminate false positives, and explain how the developer can fix the root cause.

